      hu: ["Biała Podlaska 1525-ben kapott városi rangot I. Zsigmond lengyel királytól.", "A Radziwiłł-vár kaputornya a 17. századi barokk építészet egyik remekműve.", "A városi akadémia a krakkói Jagelló Egyetem fiókintézményeként működött.", "A közeli Janów Podlaski ménes világhírű az évenkénti arab lóárveréseiről.", "A település lakossága jelenleg körülbelül 56 000 főt számlál.", "A város területén a 19. században jelentős repülőgépgyártó ipar is működött."],
      ro: ["Orașul a primit drepturi de cetate în anul 1525 de la regele Sigismund I cel Bătrân.", "Complexul Radziwiłł conține un turn de poartă baroc decorat cu sgraffito.", "Academia locală a fost fondată în 1628 și a instruit numeroși cărturari polonezi.", "Herghelia Janów Podlaski, aflată la 20 km distanță, a fost înființată în 1817.", "Biserica Sfânta Ana a fost inițial construită ca o biserică uniată (greco-catolică).", "Biała Podlaska este un important nod feroviar pe magistrala Berlin-Moscova."],
      en: ["Biała Podlaska was granted city rights in 1525 by King Sigismund I the Old.", "The Radziwiłł fortress was built using modern 17th-century Dutch fortification styles.", "The city's academy was established in 1628 as a branch of the Jagiellonian University.", "The Janów Podlaski State Stud is world-famous for its annual 'Pride of Poland' auctions.", "The city suffered significant destruction during the Swedish Deluge in the 17th century.", "Biała Podlaska was a major center for the production of textiles in the 19th century."],
